  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If Wrathful Raptors and one or more other Dinosaurs you control are dealt damage at the same time, Wrathful Raptors's ability triggers for itself and for each of those Dinosaurs, regardless of whether or not Wrathful Raptors was dealt lethal damage.",
      "oracle_id": "1ba92b64-d821-4c24-aed6-fc90d0c63c10",
      "published_at": "2023-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If lethal damage is dealt to a Dinosaur you control while you control Wrathful Raptors, Wrathful Raptors's last ability still triggers.",
      "oracle_id": "1ba92b64-d821-4c24-aed6-fc90d0c63c10",
      "published_at": "2023-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Any target that isn't a Dinosaur\" means any non-Dinosaur creature, any planeswalker or battle, or any player (no matter how old they are).",
      "oracle_id": "1ba92b64-d821-4c24-aed6-fc90d0c63c10",
      "published_at": "2023-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If multiple sources deal damage to a Dinosaur you control while you control Wrathful Raptors, most likely because multiple creatures blocked that Dinosaur, Wrathful Raptors's last ability triggers only once.",
      "oracle_id": "1ba92b64-d821-4c24-aed6-fc90d0c63c10",
      "published_at": "2023-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The total cost to cast Blasphemous Act is locked in before you pay that cost. For example, if there are three creatures on the battlefield, including one you can sacrifice to add {C}, the total cost of Blasphemous Act is {5}{R}. Then you can sacrifice the creature when you activate mana abilities just before paying the cost.",
      "oracle_id": "7a2484a9-04fd-41a0-8224-610c1c07ed10",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Blasphemous Act's ability can't reduce the total cost to cast the spell below {R}.",
      "oracle_id": "7a2484a9-04fd-41a0-8224-610c1c07ed10",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions (such as that of Blasphemous Act). The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "7a2484a9-04fd-41a0-8224-610c1c07ed10",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although players may respond to Blasphemous Act once it's been cast, once it's announced, they can't respond before the cost is calculated and paid.",
      "oracle_id": "7a2484a9-04fd-41a0-8224-610c1c07ed10",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target spell has damage divided as it was cast (like Mythos of Vadrok), the division can't be changed although the targets receiving that damage still can. The same is true of spells that distribute counters.",
      "oracle_id": "ae120613-97d6-4393-b39d-c3e6c076f5d6",
      "published_at": "2020-04-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you choose new targets for the target spell, the new targets must be legal.",
      "oracle_id": "ae120613-97d6-4393-b39d-c3e6c076f5d6",
      "published_at": "2020-04-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the target spell has a variable number of targets, you can't change how many targets it has.",
      "oracle_id": "ae120613-97d6-4393-b39d-c3e6c076f5d6",
      "published_at": "2020-04-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature loses all creature types but then gains a new creature type later in the turn, it will be that new creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "68865793-daeb-4c55-80cb-12853f9f96c4",
      "published_at": "2007-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The triggered ability on each face still works even if that damage causes this creature to die.",
      "oracle_id": "6e0b3317-394d-42cc-a350-cb5ce051787a",
      "published_at": "2021-11-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the damage causes this creature to die before the triggered ability resolves, use last known information to determine whether or not this creature had abilities such as deathtouch and lifelink. If it did, those abilities will apply to the damage",
      "oracle_id": "6e0b3317-394d-42cc-a350-cb5ce051787a",
      "published_at": "2021-11-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you discard zero cards, you will draw one card.",
      "oracle_id": "58c131f3-c623-4324-b061-9535018676b6",
      "published_at": "2021-11-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
